## Description

This function has arguments with rich, nested Markdown-relevant content.

## Usage

```r
arguments_rich(x, method, describe_arg, table_arg, pre_only, pre_with_intro,
  backtick_code, fence_collision, cr_break, multi_paragraph,
  itemize_multi_paragraph, ...)
```

## Arguments

| Argument | Description |
|:---|:---|
| `x` | A basic argument for comparison. |
| `method` | The method to use, described as a nested list: <br>- `"a"`: Use method A, the default. <br>- `"b"`: Use method B instead. |
| `describe_arg` | The method to use, described with a definition list: <br> |
| `table_arg` | The argument. See the table: <br> |
| `pre_only` |  |
| `pre_with_intro` | Example usage: <br> |
| `backtick_code` | Use `` `a` `` or ``` ``nested`` ``` for non-syntactic names. |
| `fence_collision` | Code containing a fence-like line: <br> |
| `cr_break` | First line.<br> - hyphen.<br> * asterisk.<br> + plus.<br> 1. ordered period. |
| `` `a` `` | A non-syntactic argument name with single backticks. |
| ``` ``b`` ``` | A label with a double-backtick run. |
| `multi_paragraph` | First paragraph. <br>Second paragraph of the description. |
| `itemize_multi_paragraph` | Options: <br>- First paragraph. <br>- Another item. |

## Value

Nothing of interest.

## Examples

```{r}
arguments_rich(1, "a", "a", NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, "x", "y")
```
